message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Manufacturing Substrate Regime Model"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-01-16
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.18265225"
authors:
  - family-names: Loswin
    given-names: Nawder
repository-code: "https://github.com/umaywant2/TriadicFrameworks"
abstract: >
  The Manufacturing Substrate Regime Model (MSRM) is a structural framework
  for organizing and calibrating complex manufacturing systems through
  explicitly declared operating regimes, boundary semantics, and
  operator-mediated interactions. The model is descriptive, non-physical,
  and non-optimizing, intended to support clarity and interpretability in
  extreme manufacturing environments.
keywords:
  - manufacturing systems
  - regime modeling
  - calibration structure
  - boundary semantics
  - substrate modeling
license: MIT

